# What must never enter git history.
#
# This is not the same file as .dockerignore and cannot be replaced by it: that
# one shapes the build context, this one is what stands between a `git add -A`
# and a push GitHub refuses. Three files in this tree are individually larger
# than GitHub's 100 MB blob limit, and a rejected push is the good outcome - the
# bad one is a 1.2 GB blob that lands in history and cannot be removed casually.

# --- model weights: fetched during the Docker build, never committed ---------
#   vendor/CountGD/checkpoints/checkpoint_best_regular.pth      1,250,122,522 B
#   vendor/CountGD/checkpoints/bert-base-uncased/*.safetensors    440,449,768 B
# The Dockerfile pulls both from Hugging Face at build time.
vendor/CountGD/checkpoints/

# 109 MB of an unrelated detector this service never loads - also over the limit.
yolo11x.pt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors

# --- virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------------
# Built for macOS arm64, so they are not merely large but unusable on the
# linux/amd64 image, which installs its own.
.venv/
.venv-torch/
.venv-countgd/
.env

# --- python noise ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- local runtime state -----------------------------------------------------
# The database and the survey archive live on the Railway volume at /data. A
# committed copy would ship stale jobs and rows whose media files do not exist.
.sealv/
workspace/
runs/
out/
tmp/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log

# --- sample media ------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm
*.mkv
*.avi

# --- editor / os -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# 19 MB of COCO val2017 annotations that came with the vendored CountGD clone.
# Nothing on the inference path reads it - the sole reference,
# util/static_data_path.py, points at an absolute path on the original authors'
# cluster. Already excluded from the Docker context; excluded here too because
# `railway up` uploads the working tree, so it would ride along on every deploy.
vendor/CountGD/config/instances_val2017.json
